title: Ukrainian Christmas Eve

It is traditional to serve 12 meatless dishes on Christmas Eve. (Stechyshyn, 17) The twelve dishes represent the twelve disciples. The meatless element, I believe, it to represent Jesus sharing the fish and loaves to the masses at his Sermon on the Mount.<br>

Here are some of our favorite recipes for Christmas Eve.

* [[Kutya with Barley]]
* [[Cranberry-Glazed Baked Salmon]]
* [[Tomato-Mozzarella Salad]]
* [[Green Beans with Buttered Bread Crumbs]]
* [[Varenyky]]
* [[Bigus]]
* [[Kutletky]]
* [[Fish Balls]]
* [[Kolachky]]
* [[White Borscht]] or [[Borscht]] with no meat

